<title>UK: Wellman gains ground on upbeat statement.</title>
<headline>Wellman gains ground on upbeat statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares Wellman Plc rose in active trade on Tuesday after an upbeat trading statement from the engineering and transport group, coupled with the appointment of a new finance director.</p>
<p>Recovering from sharp falls dating back to last October when the company issued a profit warning, the stock was up 3p or 13 percent at 27 by 0730 GMT in volume of 527,500 shares, the fourth most active issue in the UK market.</p>
</text>
